      "side": 1,
      "message": "I spent a while trying to figure out how to do this but never got to a satisfactory solution.  If you update a static library on incremental builds then everything downstream has to relink.  What you really want is to insert a version symbol at link time for each binary: generate_version_object -o version.o \u0026\u0026 clang -o adb adb.o version.o\n\nhttp://gareus.org/wiki/embedding_resources_in_executables and https://csl.name/post/embedding-binary-data/ have some of the ways of getting binary data into the linker.  ld -r -b binary works in linux, but obnoxiously names the symbol based on the full path to the raw file which makes it hard to use.  It also needs a bunch of flags to select the architecture, which can be hard to integrate into the command line in the build system.\n\nI\u0027ve sorta been planning some combination of ld -r -b binary and clang -sectcreate, with some platform dependent code to read it out, but it\u0027s pretty far down on my todo list so feel free to try it yourself.",
